# KSI-MLA-LET: Azure Security Contact - Alert Notifications Configured
# Azure 2.1.19: Ensure security contact email is set
# Azure 2.1.21: Ensure alert notifications are enabled

META
    esp_id `ksi-mla-let-az-security-contact-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `azure`
    criticality `high`

    title `KSI-MLA-LET: Azure Security Contact - alert notifications configured`
    description `Validates that a security contact is configured with email notifications enabled at High severity and role-based notifications active, ensuring security events are communicated to responsible personnel`
    author `security-team`
    tags `azure,security-contact,notifications,alerts`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-MLA-LET,NIST:SI-4(12),NIST:IR-6`
    control_objective `KSI-MLA-LET`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `cloud-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `3`
    recommendation `Configure security contact via az security contact create --name default --email security@example.com --alert-notifications on --alerts-admins on`

    impl_KSI_MLA_LET `Event logging and notification is validated by confirming a security contact is configured (found=true) with a valid notification email address (has_email=true), alert notifications enabled (alertNotifications.state=On) at High minimum severity, and role-based notifications active (notificationsByRole.state=On) for at least one administrative role. This ensures security alerts generated by Microsoft Defender for Cloud are delivered to designated personnel for review and response.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT contact_default
        name `default`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE st_contact_configured
        found boolean = true
        has_email boolean = true
        alert_notifications_state string = `On`
        alert_notifications_severity string = `High`
        notifications_by_role_state string = `On`
        notification_role_count int >= 1
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN az_security_contact
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF st_contact_configured
            OBJECT_REF contact_default
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
